  "answers": [
    "On the one day with sleep data, you slept about **455 minutes (7 hours 35 minutes)** in total, including a nap.\n\n- **October 2:** 420 minutes (7 hours) of overnight sleep from 11:00 PM to 7:00 AM, plus a 35-minute nap from 2:00 to 2:40 PM.\n- **Days with sleep data: 1 of 7** (October 1 through 7). October 1 and 3 through 7 have no sleep records.\n\nBecause only one day has data, there is no real \"typical day\" average. The 455-minute figure is just that single day.\n\nMissing days aren't the same as zero sleep. The local database has no sleep records for the other six days, which could mean the data hasn't been imported or synced yet, or that it wasn't recorded. The import history also shows no completed sync, so a fresh sync might add more days. I can run one if you'd like."
  ],
